OL,3,GNEWSAFamily's fears as SEND son loses
OL,4,Acollege place
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe family of a 22-year-old autistic
OL,7,Fman with severe learning disabilities
OL,8,Fsay he has taken "a massive step back"
OL,9,Fafter losing his place at a specialist
OL,10,Fcollege.
OL,12,FGeorge Mulcahy, from Shorne, spent
OL,13,Fthree years at St Piers College, where
OL,14,Fhis parents say he learnt skills
OL,15,Fincluding washing clothes, making his
OL,16,Fbed and using a dishwasher.
OL,18,FHis parents Billy and Sharon Mulcahy
OL,19,Fsay Kent County Council (KCC) has
OL,20,Fstopped funding the place and instead
OL,21,Fnamed a college that cannot meet his
OL,22,Fcomplex needs.
OL,23,APub: 01-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBLon/SE NewsCReg TVFClean Feed
FL,323,320,200,140,0,100
